.TH LUS-DEBUG 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-debug \- run a script under a debugger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus debug\fR [\-\-stdio | \-\-port N] [\-P perm]... [script [args]]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a script under the Debug Adapter Protocol, which editors such as VS Code use to set breakpoints, step through code, and inspect variables.
An editor starts this command itself.
Debugger describes the features.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-stdio\fR
Read requests from standard input and write replies to standard output.
This is the default.
.TP
\fB\-\-port N\fR
Accept one client on \fB127.0.0.1:N\fR, for an editor that connects to a running adapter.
.TP
\fB\-P perm\fR, \fB\-\-pledge perm\fR
Grant a permission to the program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The session ended.
.TP
1
The protocol channel cannot be opened or the session failed.
.TP
2
An option is malformed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-debug, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
